- Yeah, the guy flipped out. So what?

467
00:39:11.716 --> 00:39:14.468
So that Oakland P.D. detective,
what's-his-name, he never bought it.

468
00:39:14.552 --> 00:39:17.637
Cabby had no criminal record,
no history of mental illness.

469
00:39:17.722 --> 00:39:20.182
Pops three people, then himself?

470
00:39:21.601 --> 00:39:26.271
Anyway, that detective always thought
there was someone else in that cab.

471
00:39:56.886 --> 00:39:59.471
I never learned to listen to jazz.

472
00:40:00.848 --> 00:40:05.018
It's off melody. Behind the notes.
Not what's expected.

473
00:40:05.103 --> 00:40:08.230
- Improvising, like tonight.
- Like tonight?

474
00:40:33.005 --> 00:40:35.090
Most people, 10 years from now,

475
00:40:35.174 --> 00:40:37.592
same job, same place, same routine,
everything the same.

476
00:40:37.677 --> 00:40:40.387
Just keeping it safe
over and over and over.

477
00:40:40.471 --> 00:40:42.305
Ten years from now.

478
00:40:42.807 --> 00:40:46.518
Man, you don't know where you'll be
10 minutes from now.

479
00:40:47.353 --> 00:40:48.603
Do you?

480
00:41:04.036 --> 00:41:08.290
- Who is that on the trumpet?
- That's Daniel, baby. He's the owner.

481
00:41:10.042 --> 00:41:13.712
He's terrific. Would you be so kind
as to invite him over after his set?

482
00:41:13.796 --> 00:41:17.007
- I gotta buy him a drink.
- Sure thing, darling.

483
00:41:24.390 --> 00:41:28.476
No, now, see, I was about 19,
bussing tables right here.

484
00:41:28.561 --> 00:41:31.396
The money wasn't shit,
but that wasn't the point.

485
00:41:31.480 --> 00:41:34.316
It was about being around the music.
And I was.

486
00:41:34.400 --> 00:41:35.984
I mean, take this one night.

487
00:41:36.068 --> 00:41:39.279
July 22nd, 1964.
Who you think walks through that door?

488
00:41:39.363 --> 00:41:41.072
Bye, baby.

489
00:41:41.157 --> 00:41:43.575
Miles Davis. That's right.

490
00:41:43.659 --> 00:41:44.868
- In the flesh?
- That's right.

491
00:41:44.952 --> 00:41:48.330
I'm talking about, through those doors,
the coolest man on the planet.

492
00:41:48.414 --> 00:41:49.706
Jesus.

493
00:41:49.790 --> 00:41:52.334
Anyway, he had been
at a recording session

494
00:41:52.418 --> 00:41:56.421
up at Columbia, up on Vine.
So Miles comes through that door.

495
00:41:56.505 --> 00:42:01.176
Before you know it, he's up on
the bandstand, jamming with the band.

496
00:42:01.260 --> 00:42:03.887
- Well, it had to be...
- Oh, it was scary.

497
00:42:03.971 --> 00:42:06.514
I mean, the dude was so focused, man.

498
00:42:06.599 --> 00:42:09.017
Plus, he was kind of
a scary cat anyway, man.

499
00:42:09.101 --> 00:42:10.518
I mean, everybody and their mama knew

500
00:42:10.603 --> 00:42:13.647
that you don't just come up
and talk to Miles Davis.

501
00:42:13.731 --> 00:42:18.151
I mean, he may have looked like
he was chilling, but he was absorbed.

502
00:42:18.236 --> 00:42:22.447
This one young, hip couple, one of them
tried to shake his hand one day.

503
00:42:22.531 --> 00:42:25.533
And the guy says, "Hi, my name is..."

504
00:42:25.618 --> 00:42:28.161
Miles said, "Get the fuck out of my face,
you jive motherfucker.

505
00:42:28.246 --> 00:42:30.789
"Take your silly bitch with you."

506
00:42:32.083 --> 00:42:34.834
You know? That's...
That was Miles, man.

507
00:42:34.919 --> 00:42:39.547
That's the way he was when he was
in his musical headspace. Fierce.

508
00:42:39.632 --> 00:42:41.132
But did you get to talk to him?

509
00:42:41.217 --> 00:42:42.801
- Better than that.
- No.

510
00:42:42.885 --> 00:42:46.471
- I played for about 20 minutes.
- Unbelievable.

511
00:42:46.555 --> 00:42:48.473
- How'd you do?
- How'd I do?

512
00:42:48.557 --> 00:42:51.559
Well, you really ain't shit when
you're playing next to Miles Davis.

513
00:42:51.644 --> 00:42:53.853
But he carried my ass.

514
00:42:53.938 --> 00:42:57.232
- What'd he say?
- He said one word, "Cool."

515
00:42:57.858 --> 00:42:59.234
- "Cool"?
- Yeah.

516
00:42:59.318 --> 00:43:00.819
- That's it?
- Yeah.

517
00:43:00.903 --> 00:43:03.196
That meant, "Good, but not ready."

518
00:43:03.281 --> 00:43:05.949
It meant, "Look me up when you are."

519
00:43:06.534 --> 00:43:08.410
- Did you?
- No.

520
00:43:09.287 --> 00:43:12.414
I got drafted
and got into some other things,

521
00:43:12.498 --> 00:43:16.960
and by the time I got back to music,
the season had passed.

522
00:43:18.004 --> 00:43:20.880
But, you know, I was born in 1945,

523
00:43:20.965 --> 00:43:24.843
but that night was
the moment of my conception.

524
00:43:24.927 --> 00:43:28.054
- Right here in this room.
- Crowd's not here now.

525
00:43:28.139 --> 00:43:31.308
Well, jazz ain't the draw
that it used to be.

526
00:43:33.185 --> 00:43:35.103
What a great story.

527
00:43:35.813 --> 00:43:39.858
I gotta tell the people in Culiacàn
and Cartagena that story.

528
00:43:53.080 --> 00:43:56.333
You know the folks in Culiacàn
and Cartagena?

529
00:43:56.417 --> 00:43:57.834
Afraid so.

530
00:43:59.587 --> 00:44:02.047
Man, just when I thought
you were a cool guy.

531
00:44:02.131 --> 00:44:05.592
I am a cool guy,
with a job I contracted to do.

532
00:44:05.676 --> 00:44:07.802
Come on, Vincent,
give the dude a pass.

533
00:44:07.887 --> 00:44:09.387
- I'm working here.
- No, listen. You the one

534
00:44:09.472 --> 00:44:11.264
sitting here talking about improvisation.

535
00:44:11.349 --> 00:44:13.224
You like the guy, you like how he plays.

536
00:44:13.309 --> 00:44:15.852
- Let's just play a little jazz. Come on.
- Improv...

537
00:44:15.936 --> 00:44:18.313
That's funny, coming from you.

538
00:44:23.986 --> 00:44:26.571
How's this? I'll ask a question.

539
00:44:26.655 --> 00:44:29.574
- What question?
- A jazz question.

540
00:44:30.284 --> 00:44:32.786
Now, you get it right, we roll.

541
00:44:34.121 --> 00:44:36.081
You disappear tonight.

542
00:44:36.874 --> 00:44:38.666
If I walk out of here tonight,

543
00:44:38.751 --> 00:44:42.754
I will go so far away,
it'll be just like I was dead.

544
00:44:42.838 --> 00:44:44.214
And one more thing.

545
00:44:44.298 --> 00:44:47.926
These people and their rep here, Felix,

546
00:44:48.010 --> 00:44:50.428
well, you tell them I'm sorry.

547
00:44:50.513 --> 00:44:55.266
You tell them I had to.
They laid a grant of immunity on me.

548
00:44:55.351 --> 00:44:58.478
I was compelled.
It was either play ball or go back inside.

549
00:44:58.562 --> 00:45:01.523
And I'm not going back inside.

550
00:45:04.777 --> 00:45:06.069
Yeah.

551
00:45:09.407 --> 00:45:11.116
Lay it on me.

552
00:45:12.201 --> 00:45:14.035
Where did Miles learn music?

553
00:45:14.120 --> 00:45:15.954
I know everything
there is to know about Miles.

554
00:45:16.038 --> 00:45:17.455
Then let's have it.

555
00:45:17.540 --> 00:45:20.667
Music school.
He got into music school, right?

556
00:45:20.751 --> 00:45:23.586
His father was a dentist, East St Louis.

557
00:45:23.671 --> 00:45:25.588
Invested in agriculture,
made plenty of money.

558
00:45:25.673 --> 00:45:29.050
He sent Miles
to Juilliard School of Music,

559
00:45:29.135 --> 00:45:31.469
New York, 1945.

560
00:45:31.554 --> 00:45:32.762
Man.

561
00:45:47.278 --> 00:45:49.070
Dropped out of Juilliard
after less than a year.

562
00:45:49.155 --> 00:45:51.573
Tracked down Charlie Parker
on 52nd Street,

563
00:45:51.657 --> 00:45:54.617
who mentored him
for the next three years.

564
00:46:17.099 --> 00:46:20.602
- Hey.
- No. No, I'm done.

565
00:46:20.686 --> 00:46:22.604
- Find you another cab.
- Max.

566
00:46:22.688 --> 00:46:25.440
Leave me alone. I'm collateral anyway.

567
00:46:32.239 --> 00:46:33.948
I am not playing.

568
00:46:36.452 --> 00:46:38.286
You played him, man.

569
00:46:39.788 --> 00:46:43.708
He got the answer right,
would you have let him go?

570
00:46:47.171 --> 00:46:50.298
This is 102. This is 102. Max?

571
00:46:50.382 --> 00:46:53.009
- What is it with this guy?
- Max?

572
00:47:03.103 --> 00:47:05.939
- You hassling my driver again?
- Who are you?

573
00:47:06.023 --> 00:47:08.566
The same guy you talked to last time.

574
00:47:08.651 --> 00:47:12.070
Max's mother's driving me crazy.
Put him on the line, please.

575
00:47:12.154 --> 00:47:13.530
Hang on.

576
00:47:14.782 --> 00:47:16.199
Carefully.

577
00:47:18.327 --> 00:47:19.452
Yeah.

578
00:47:19.537 --> 00:47:20.995
Your mother's calling every 10 minutes.

579
00:47:21.080 --> 00:47:23.456
Why didn't you show?
Are you all right? Where are you?

580
00:47:23.541 --> 00:47:25.124
Show for what?

581
00:47:26.669 --> 00:47:28.336
Tell her I can't make it tonight.

582
00:47:28.420 --> 00:47:30.797
I'm not related to you.
You tell her yourself.

583
00:47:30.881 --> 00:47:32.590
Show up for what?

584
00:47:34.843 --> 00:47:36.678
She's in the hospital.

585
00:47:36.762 --> 00:47:39.264
- You visit every night?
- Yeah. What difference does it make?

586
00:47:39.348 --> 00:47:42.183
- You don't show up, it breaks routine.
- So?

587
00:47:42.268 --> 00:47:46.104
So people start looking for you, this cab.
That's not good.

588
00:47:47.982 --> 00:47:50.650
I'm not taking you to see my mother.

589
00:47:51.485 --> 00:47:54.404
Since when was any of this negotiable?

590
00:48:00.911 --> 00:48:03.454
Two paces ahead, one to the left.

591
00:48:08.919 --> 00:48:10.837
Hey. Flowers?

592
00:48:11.922 --> 00:48:15.216
It's a waste of money.
Won't mean a thing to her.

593
00:48:16.343 --> 00:48:19.554
She carried you in her womb
for nine months.

594
00:48:23.934 --> 00:48:26.561
People buy flowers. Buy flowers.

595
00:48:26.645 --> 00:48:28.938
Excuse me. Keep the change.

596
00:48:40.451 --> 00:48:42.660
Hold that elevator, please.

597
00:48:45.497 --> 00:48:47.373
- Floor?
- Five. Thanks.

598
00:48:58.719 --> 00:49:02.221
- Having a good night?
- Maso maso. You?

599
00:49:11.565 --> 00:49:12.940
Excuse me.

600
00:49:47.267 --> 00:49:48.601
Hey, Ma.

601
00:49:50.646 --> 00:49:54.023
- I've been calling and calling.
- Yeah, well, I got caught up at work.

602
00:49:54.108 --> 00:49:56.192
Why couldn't you call me
on the telephone?

603
00:49:56.276 --> 00:49:59.112
I'm lying here wondering
if something terrible happened to you.

604
00:49:59.196 --> 00:50:00.488
I brought you flowers.

605
00:50:00.572 --> 00:50:02.949
- What am I gonna do with flowers?
- Cheer up.

606
00:50:03.033 --> 00:50:04.325
How?

607
00:50:04.410 --> 00:50:09.288
By worrying that you spend money
on stuff that's just gonna wilt and die?

608
00:50:09.373 --> 00:50:11.082
See what I mean?

609
00:50:11.166 --> 00:50:13.251
I didn't buy you the flowers, Mom.
He did.

610
00:50:13.335 --> 00:50:14.585
Who?

611
00:50:19.591 --> 00:50:22.343
Why didn't you tell me
we had company?

612
00:50:24.346 --> 00:50:27.974
What's your name?
Sorry my son is rude.

613
00:50:28.058 --> 00:50:30.184
No harm done, ma'am.

614
00:50:30.269 --> 00:50:32.770
You paid for my flowers?

615
00:50:32.855 --> 00:50:34.647
They're beautiful.

616
00:50:42.948 --> 00:50:44.365
Well, Max?

617
00:50:48.162 --> 00:50:51.956
Mother, this is Vincent.
Vincent, this is my mother, Ida.

618
00:50:55.085 --> 00:50:57.378
I'm very happy to meet you,
Mrs. Durocher.

619
00:50:57.463 --> 00:50:59.213
Oh, just call me Ida.

620
00:50:59.298 --> 00:51:03.342
Ida. I was with Max when he got the call.

621
00:51:03.427 --> 00:51:05.553
And you came all the way
over here to see me?

622
00:51:05.637 --> 00:51:08.848
- It's nothing, ma'am.
- Tell my son.

623
00:51:08.932 --> 00:51:13.019
You have to hold a gun to his head
to make him do anything.

624
00:51:13.103 --> 00:51:16.481
You must be one of Max's
important clients.

625
00:51:16.565 --> 00:51:21.027
Client? I... You know, I like
to think of myself as his friend.

626
00:51:21.111 --> 00:51:22.862
Max never had many friends.

627
00:51:22.946 --> 00:51:25.823
Always talking to himself in the mirror.
It's unhealthy.

628
00:51:25.908 --> 00:51:28.367
Mom, how many times I got to ask you?
Please don't do that.

629
00:51:28.452 --> 00:51:29.535
Do what?

630
00:51:29.620 --> 00:51:32.705
Don't talk about me like
I'm not right here in the room here.

631
00:51:32.790 --> 00:51:34.081
What's he saying?

632
00:51:34.166 --> 00:51:37.752
He says he's standing right here,
in the room here.

633
00:51:37.836 --> 00:51:39.796
Yes, you are.

634
00:51:39.880 --> 00:51:42.757
- He's sensitive.
- I know.

635
00:51:42.841 --> 00:51:44.509
But I'm sure you're very proud of him.

636
00:51:44.593 --> 00:51:48.554
Of course I'm proud.
He started with nothing, you know.

637
00:51:48.639 --> 00:51:51.682
- Look at him today. Here, Vegas...
- Mom. Mom.

638
00:51:51.767 --> 00:51:54.977
Mom. Mom, he is not interested
in hearing about all that, okay?

639
00:51:55.062 --> 00:51:57.438
I came to see you, I saw you.
You look good, let's go.

640
00:51:57.523 --> 00:52:00.983
No, no, no. No, no, no.
I am very interested, Ida. Please.

641
00:52:01.068 --> 00:52:03.945
- Limousine companies.
- Is that right?

642
00:52:04.029 --> 00:52:06.364
He drives famous people around.

643
00:52:06.448 --> 00:52:10.785
Famous people. Limousine companies.
Now that's quite an achievement.

644
00:52:10.869 --> 00:52:12.870
What did you say your name was again?

645
00:52:12.955 --> 00:52:14.872
My name's Vincent, ma'am.

646
00:52:15.666 --> 00:52:19.210
- Visit again?
- No, I'm just in town tonight.

647
00:52:19.294 --> 00:52:21.671
- When you come back.
- Sure.

648
00:52:39.648 --> 00:52:40.815
Max!

649
00:53:24.735 --> 00:53:25.943
Don't!

650
00:53:55.265 --> 00:53:59.143
All of my prep was in there.
You are screwing with my work.

651
00:54:04.650 --> 00:54:06.692
Let's see what else you can do.

652
00:54:10.656 --> 00:54:14.575
Well, I've had four come in tonight.
Maybe one's your guy.

653
00:54:19.081 --> 00:54:21.666
No, not Ramone. Let's see this one.

654
00:54:27.589 --> 00:54:28.839
No, next.

655
00:54:28.924 --> 00:54:32.259
Okay, you know, something's funny
about this, though, you know?

656
00:54:32.344 --> 00:54:36.430
These three all came in within
half an hour of each other, right?

657
00:54:36.515 --> 00:54:40.977
The kid and that last guy,
both done by the same shooter, I think.

658
00:54:41.895 --> 00:54:44.647
- Why do you say that?
- Wound pattern.

659
00:54:45.857 --> 00:54:48.818
Two in the sternum, one in the head.

660
00:54:48.902 --> 00:54:52.279
This guy, he's shooting tight
groups too, all right? Check this out.

661
00:54:52.364 --> 00:54:55.491
Double taps a couple millimeters apart.

662
00:54:55.575 --> 00:54:57.368
Let's see this one.

663
00:55:06.670 --> 00:55:08.629
See what I mean?

664
00:55:10.382 --> 00:55:13.342
- Holy shit. Can I use your phone?
- Yeah.

665
00:55:19.641 --> 00:55:21.767
Come on, come on, wake up.

666
00:55:36.742 --> 00:55:38.743
- Hello.
- Hey, it's Fanning.

667
00:55:38.827 --> 00:55:41.203
I'm still down here at the morgue
at Sisters of Charity.

668
00:55:41.288 --> 00:55:43.622
Those John Does didn't pan out,
but you're never gonna guess

669
00:55:43.707 --> 00:55:46.333
- who I got here in the meat locker.
- Who?

670
00:55:46.418 --> 00:55:50.546
Sylvester Clarke, criminal attorney
turned lawyer-criminal.

671
00:55:50.630 --> 00:55:55.426
Including Ramone, who he represented,
who's still missing.

672
00:55:55.510 --> 00:55:58.679
The both of whom are in the
exotic-substances business together.

673
00:55:58.764 --> 00:56:02.391
There's something going on,
and I don't think the feds know about it.

674
00:56:02.476 --> 00:56:05.770
Tell you what, stay on your cell phone.
I got the ASAC's phone.

675
00:56:05.854 --> 00:56:08.022
I'll hook up with you in 30 minutes.

676
00:56:08.106 --> 00:56:09.273
Good.

677
00:56:15.572 --> 00:56:17.406
You're gonna go to a place
called El Rodeo.

678
00:56:17.491 --> 00:56:19.492
It's on Washington Boulevard
in Pico Rivera.

679
00:56:19.576 --> 00:56:22.328
- Where at on Washington?
- Look it up.

680
00:56:27.334 --> 00:56:28.751
Limos, huh?

681
00:56:29.753 --> 00:56:31.295
Don't start.

682
00:56:31.379 --> 00:56:33.714
Hey, I'm not the one lying to my mother.

683
00:56:33.799 --> 00:56:36.675
She hears what she wants to hear.
I don't disillusion her.

684
00:56:36.760 --> 00:56:39.011
Yeah, right.
Maybe she hears what you tell her.

685
00:56:39.096 --> 00:56:40.971
Whatever I tell her
is never good enough anyway.

686
00:56:41.056 --> 00:56:43.182
It's always been that way.

687
00:56:44.184 --> 00:56:47.436
- So what's at El Rodeo?
- Just drive.

688
00:56:49.106 --> 00:56:51.315
They project onto you their flaws.

689
00:56:51.399 --> 00:56:54.985
What they don't like about themselves,
their lives, whatever.

690
00:56:55.070 --> 00:56:57.196
They rank on you instead.

691
00:56:58.865 --> 00:57:01.951
- How do you know?
- I had a father like that.

692
00:57:03.245 --> 00:57:04.537
Mothers are worse.

693
00:57:04.621 --> 00:57:07.289
Wouldn't know.
My mother died before I remember.

694
00:57:07.374 --> 00:57:09.708
What happened to your father?

695
00:57:10.168 --> 00:57:12.169
Hated everything I did.

696
00:57:13.296 --> 00:57:17.758
Got drunk, beat me up, foster homes.
Went back with him. Like that.

697
00:57:20.762 --> 00:57:22.138
Then what?

698
00:57:25.183 --> 00:57:26.725
I killed him.

699
00:57:28.436 --> 00:57:29.770
I was 12.

700
00:57:37.988 --> 00:57:39.488
I'm kidding.

701
00:57:42.450 --> 00:57:44.535
He died of liver disease.

702
00:57:47.080 --> 00:57:49.623
- Well, I'm sorry.
- No, you're not.

703
00:58:05.182 --> 00:58:07.474
So what is this
"driving a cab temporarily"?

704
00:58:07.559 --> 00:58:11.395
- It's just all bullshit, huh?
- It is not bullshit.

705
00:58:11.479 --> 00:58:13.397
Twelve years isn't temporary, Max.

706
00:58:13.481 --> 00:58:17.193
Gotta get the cash together.
Insurance, bonds, maintenance, tires.

